; orpot flower holder for the net3 pot (top plate, fin A1 (slots from top), fin A2 (slots from top), fin B1 (slots from bottom), fin B2 (slots from bottom))
; pot: 3" net cup, TYPICAL catalogue size (NOT measured): lip 80, body 72 under the lip, bottom 55, height 75. Caliper yours and pass --net-* before cutting
; material ply3: t 2.63 mm, slots drawn 2.63 mm, kerf 0.1 mm
; geometry (mm): lift 20.0, c 16.0, plate_top 91.0, fin_top 88.37, h 32.41, tab 8.0, gap 4.0, halflap 10.0, hole 73.09, plate_d 165.7
; X0 Y0 = bottom-left corner of the stock
; quickcut: GRBL diode-laser cut, static M3, warmup on every path
; cut: ply3 100% (S1000 of 1000) F350 x1; warmup 1000ms = 5.8mm
; every cut: warmup wiggle (half the warmup out and back), then the passes;
; closed loops overlap the warmup distance past their start; middle-out order
;
;HEAD: laser
;MATERIAL: ply3
;LASER_MODE: static  (M3, constant power; assumes Z already at focus)

$32=1   ; GRBL laser mode (assumes firmware $30=1000)
G21     ; mm
G90     ; absolute
M5      ; laser off

; --- cut 1/50 (loop, 38 pts) ---
; frame: rapid trace of the job's extent, laser OFF: x 0.000 to 358.700, y 0.000 to 263.700
; (an endstop or alarm here means the job won't fit from this zero: nothing has been marked yet)
M5
G0 X0.000 Y0.000
G0 X358.700 Y0.000
G0 X358.700 Y263.700
G0 X0.000 Y263.700
G0 X0.000 Y0.000

